    "result_text": "The build succeeds and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the rule that rejects creating an owner whose lower-cased email is already used by another owner, responding with **409 Conflict**. I followed the existing conventions in the codebase (mirroring the telephone/household duplicate handling):\n\n1. **`DuplicateEmailException`** (`rest/error/`) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` carrying the conflicting email, parallel to `DuplicateTelephoneException`.\n\n2. **`EmailUniquenessValidator`** (`rest/validation/`) \u2014 a `@Component` with a single responsibility: given a normalized email, it skips absent (null/blank) emails since email is optional, otherwise compares its lower-cased form case-insensitively against all existing owners and throws `DuplicateEmailException` on a match. This mirrors `HouseholdDuplicateValidator`'s in-memory approach and reuses `ClinicService.findAllOwners()`.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1`** \u2014 injected the new validator and invoked `emailUniquenessValidator.validate(...)` right after the email is normalized, so the check runs against the canonical lower-cased value.\n\n4. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` mapping `DuplicateEmailException` to a 409 `ProblemDetail` naming the `email` field, consistent with the other duplicate handlers.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
